{%- comment -%}
  Resolves which pack type a product is, for the enrolment-vs-reorder colour
  block (ClickUp 869etbgcb).

  Context: the word "Enrolment" is being removed from pack names, so the colour
  block is the ONLY signal telling a customer which pack type they are looking
  at. It therefore has to resolve the same way on every surface — collection
  page, homepage cards and PDP — which is why the logic lives in one snippet
  rather than being repeated per template.

  Outputs a bare token, nothing else. Capture it in the caller:

    {%- capture pack_type -%}{% render 'pack-type', product: product %}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign pack_type = pack_type | strip -%}

  Returns 'enrolment', 'reorder', or an empty string when the product is
  neither (e.g. a single bottle), in which case callers render no colour block
  and the card keeps its current appearance.

  Resolution order:
    1. product.metafields.ava.pack_type  — authoritative. Set per product in
       Shopify admin, so pack classification never needs a theme deploy.
    2. Collection handles from the theme settings, as a fallback for products
       whose metafield is not populated yet.

  Accepts:
    product - REQUIRED. The product object.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign resolved = ''

  # 1. Metafield wins. Tolerate the spellings people actually type.
  assign mf_value = product.metafields.ava.pack_type.value | default: product.metafields.ava.pack_type
  assign mf_value = mf_value | downcase | strip

  if mf_value != blank
    if mf_value contains 'enrol'
      assign resolved = 'enrolment'
    elsif mf_value contains 'reorder' or mf_value contains 'maintenance' or mf_value contains 'repeat'
      assign resolved = 'reorder'
    endif
  endif

  # 2. Fall back to collection membership while metafields are still being
  #    populated. Handles are theme settings so they stay editable.
  if resolved == blank
    assign enrol_handles = settings.pack_enrolment_collections | default: '' | downcase | split: ','
    assign reorder_handles = settings.pack_reorder_collections | default: '' | downcase | split: ','

    for collection in product.collections
      assign handle = collection.handle | downcase

      for candidate in enrol_handles
        assign candidate_handle = candidate | strip
        if handle == candidate_handle
          assign resolved = 'enrolment'
          break
        endif
      endfor
      if resolved != blank
        break
      endif

      for candidate in reorder_handles
        assign candidate_handle = candidate | strip
        if handle == candidate_handle
          assign resolved = 'reorder'
          break
        endif
      endfor
      if resolved != blank
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}
{{- resolved -}}
